  "id": "nearby-happy",
  "description": "Nearby approval, the quiet case (WIRE-CONTRACT-V5 §12.11.5). D, a device with no way to sign in, posts its signing and agreement keys with a pkey-proof/1 nearby-start proof and gets a request handle (nr_…, 300 s) and the poll interval (3 s). Its first poll is pending; a second inside the interval is 429 slow_down. M, a signed-in device of the account on the same network, posts approve with the handle, D's two keys and a nearby-approve proof by its own registered key: the account has exactly one licence with a free seat, so it is bound with no further tap and the answer names D's label. D's next poll, after the interval, answers the device token once (D never held a grant). Poll proofs are by the key D sent on start.",
